From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: a control buffer's release decided before its callback

The interrupt DPC ran a finished control buffer's callback, then read the buffer's auto_release. The commands that
wait for their answer (blob creation, display info, EDID, capsets, long backing lists) have the callback set an
event and release the buffer themselves: woken, the thread could release (and free) it before the DPC read the flag
from the freed buffer, and release it again - a pool double free (3DMark Vantage: bugcheck 0x13A,
KERNEL_MODE_HEAP_CORRUPTION, in a gVIO block). The flag is read before the callback.
---
--- a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_adapter.cpp
+++ b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_adapter.cpp
@@ -1322,11 +1322,14 @@
                               resp->ctx_id,
                               pcmd->type));
                 }
+                // Read before the callback: a buffer that isn't released here belongs to the thread the callback
+                // wakes, which may release it (and free it) before this goes on
+                bool release = pvbuf->auto_release;
                 if (pvbuf->complete_cb != NULL)
                 {
                     pvbuf->complete_cb(pvbuf->complete_ctx);
                 }
-                if (pvbuf->auto_release)
+                if (release)
                 {
                     ctrlQueue.ReleaseBuffer(pvbuf);
                 }
